## Risks
- Full baseline/squash is intentionally staged: archiving 213 migrations without production backup, row-count audit, and DROP/KEEP signoff is the highest-risk part of the review.
- Generated Supabase types may be hard to regenerate if local DB is not resettable; fallback manual edits must be minimal and carefully reviewed.
- `integration_sync_runs.source_type` currently uses `order_source_type`; adding more source keys must match existing enum values (`shopsite`, `integra`) or the migration will fail.
- Realtime payloads from `integration_sync_runs` do not match `MigrationLogEntry`; client-side normalization is required to avoid UI runtime issues.
- Seed inserts must use stable UUIDs and `ON CONFLICT` clauses; otherwise repeated `db:reset`/seed runs can fail.
- Do not drop `products.shopsite_*` or `migration_log` in this PR; existing production DBs need a separate destructive cleanup after verification.
